# Stray output tree: a builder run from this directory used to resolve the workspace
# from cwd and write here instead of the sibling repo. Fixed in traust-engine 0.6.4;
# ignored so a mis-invocation cannot be committed again.
/progress-tracker/

# Security-data feed cache — third-party licensed data (CC-BY/CC0),
# rebuildable by re-fetching, and a different provenance class from
# anything we author. Never commit: ~6 MB reached this repo's history
# via analysis-results/feeds/ before the cache moved out (2026-08-25).
# Location is config-driven — FEEDS_CACHE_DIR, default
# <workspace>/progress-tracker/feeds.
/analysis-results/feeds/
/progress-tracker/

# Orphaned working tree from the 2026-08-26 skill restructure: 9.6 GB of target
# clones (embedded git repos) and 394 MB of Java batch logs. Never repo content;
# 'make clone' recreates the clones. Retired per
# progress-tracker/plans/fuzz-artifact-relocation-plan.md step 5.
harnessing/pqc-readiness/bin/
harnessing/pqc-readiness/scripts/

# mine-ledger rule-drafts are generated output (emit_rule_drafts.py default
# --out-dir); they carry per-finding provenance and regenerate from the ledger,
# so they are never committed. Deployments keep their copies in their private
# configuration repository.
harnessing/mine-ledger/rule-drafts/

# /graphify knowledge-graph output (graph.json, graph.html, GRAPH_REPORT.md,
# extraction cache and manifest). Generated from the tree by the graphify
# skill and rebuilt on demand, so it is never repo content.
graphify-out/
